[ceiling] These are the three required support-off horizontal rail bridges at Z 4.04, spanning 32.70 mm clear between 3.00 mm end posts; rail section is 3.60 by 2.40 mm. The moving floors end at Z 2.60, leaving 1.44 mm fixed lower air. Current native first rail nozzle Z 4.28 minus 0.24 mm model step gives underside 4.04, and no deposits fill the release gap. The combined assembly is one print with four separately closed bodies; physical bridge sag, initial release and sliding force remain unmeasured.
alternatives: A tapered rail underside or added corbel reduces bridge demand while changing the fixed lower-contact/air geometry. Raising the rail and moving roofs together permits more thickness but changes the common layer schedule and needs a new travel/clearance review. A separately inserted rigid rail avoids this bridge while removing the print-in-place release question.
