[ceiling] This is the 13 by 14.15 by 1.60 mm touch flag over the 6 mm wide eye: approximately 3.50 mm projection per X side and 3.85 mm forward projection. It is an accessible handle/finish feature, separate from the 0.24/0.48/0.72 upper-release planes. Existing native first flag layers use Bridge and Overhang-wall deposits with supports off; these small cantilevers remain an unprinted finish/handling risk, not a missing-path finding.
alternatives: A roughly 3.85 mm taller tapered shoulder can grow to the same handle width above the existing eye roof while preserving the release planes, but increases shutter height and needs a new travel/neighbor-clearance review. A narrower flag removes the side projection but gives less touch/pull area. A separately attached larger handle adds a joint and another part to the captive assembly.
file: hardware/printed-parts/calibration/soda-studies/print-assemblies/pip-base.step
