[ceiling] This is the captive eye's required solid-skin upper release ceiling, with 2.40 mm roof stock. Leaf-only lint measures the drop to its own 2.60 mm floor; the four-body manufacturing assembly places the fixed rail top at Z 6.44, giving CAD roof air 0.24/0.48/0.72 mm for Q24/Q48/Q72. Native roof nozzle Z 6.92/7.16/7.40 minus the 0.24 mm model step gives the same nominal underside/air. No model/support deposits occupy the release windows; physical strand sag, contact and release remain unmeasured. The solid skins are a distinct comparison from sparse support interfaces.
alternatives: A sloped or open roof avoids this ceiling but removes capture or changes the flat upper-contact test. Raising the roof to a larger gap is a different comparison rung, not a correction inferred from this leaf-only drop. A separately assembled eye can use thicker open sections while giving up the print-in-place release question.
