[thin] These picks bound the real 0.20 mm wide, 0.12 mm high upper rim between the datum rear edge Y 58.30 and the basin window front edge Y 58.50. It sits on 6.08 mm of continuous stock and has no bearing or capture function. Its thin upper edge can be read as a surface/printing detail; it is not the fixed 3.60 by 2.40 mm rail or the 0.35 per-face running clearance. Physical rim reproduction is unrecorded.
alternatives: Leaving the entire 6.20 mm area flat removes the small rim with more continuous stock but removes the shallow reveal feature. Extending the recess to Y 58.50 removes the rim while changing its rear boundary. A 0.24 mm deep, edge-aligned recess is more pronounced on the layer grid and changes the finish datum; none of these substitutes establish shutter release.
