[thin] These shortest approaches occur from the full 6.20 mm basin's bore or outer edge toward a top marking/corner. They do not define a 2–3 mm nominal basin wall. The through bores are diameter 4.40 and 6.65 mm at X -78/+78, Y 40, and the raised values identify nominal holes only; the short bearing lengths/entrances of production organizers are not reproduced. Hole fit, marking readability and basin strength are unmeasured.
alternatives: Moving values farther from bores/outer edges enlarges these local distances but expands or rearranges the reading field. Widening/thickening the basin adds stock and changes the sculpture footprint or bed schedule. Separate bore gauges can have longer production contact lengths but add parts and a different hole-fit specimen.
