[thin] These oblique 2.188 mm closest approaches occur at the rail ends where the Z 4.04 underside meets the Z 6.20 basin/window edge. The rail itself is 2.40 mm thick with 3.60 mm Y width and continuous 3.00 mm end posts. They are rail-to-basin terminating corners, not an isolated 2.188 mm fin or a different upper/lower release gap. This stock has no physical load or lifetime qualification.
alternatives: Thickening the rail downward to 3.00 mm reduces the fixed 1.44 mm lower air unless the floor is moved. Widening the rail needs a larger eye opening to preserve 0.35 mm per-face running air. Larger outward end pads preserve the active rail but occupy more window/travel access and need a new collision review.
