[thin] This combined-only 2.885 mm pair is a closest approach through air between two separate bodies: the basin recess edge(-54.417,55,6.195) and Q24 front flag corner(-54.417,55,9.080). It is neither material thickness nor the active upper-release gap. The exact four-body STL and separately named native volumes preserve that separation; the thickness method does not attribute a closest pair to connected-body material.
alternatives: A roughly 3.85 mm taller tapered handle shoulder increases this clearance while retaining the active eye roof/rail release planes, but adds height and needs a new travel/collision review. A narrower handle adds edge air with less touch area. Larger active roof gaps are different comparison rungs and do not repair a material defect inferred from this cross-body reading.
