click: x=-54.417 y=55.000 z=9.080

[thin] These opposite surfaces bound the 3.00 mm nominal post/column stock rooted in the 6.20 mm basin, including the shutter end stops and grip-side support. They are functional storage/capture stock, distinct from the release-air ladders and authentic flexure skins. The current parked/removal paths are sampled nominal geometry; this section has no handling-load or lifetime acceptance.
alternatives: Wider 4.00 or 6.00 mm posts increase stock outward but reduce window/travel access or require new spacing and collision review. A continuous broad rear wall backs the rails but encloses their release windows. A separate stand carries the grip column with another part and contact configuration.
